# Spec §5.8 (Reanudar), with §5.2, §5.3, §5.5–§5.7, §6.1 (order, checkbox),
# §6.2 (Última vez, change of kind) and §6.3 (Historial).
# Reanudar stores reanudadaEn = now and removes paused. From then on the
# recurring task is evaluated as if just created at reanudadaEn: with creadaEn =
# reanudadaEn and without the completions with completadoEn earlier than
# reanudadaEn (one with completadoEn equal to reanudadaEn counts). So:
#   relative: pending on resume (never completed);
#   calendar: pending if today is an occurrence day; otherwise waiting
#     until the next one, with progress from reanudadaEn;
#   with a schedule, §5.5–§5.7 with that creadaEn; an occurrence whose window
#     closed before reanudadaEn (to <= reanudadaEn) does not count as
#     missed: it stays waiting until the next one, not overdue.
# What happened during the pause does not count as overdue. Earlier
# completions remain in Historial and in Última vez. The filter is
# permanent: it still applies after changes of kind or mode, until the
# next resume.
# reanudadaEn only applies to recurring tasks: a one-off task ignores it. Changing
# a paused recurring task to one-off resumes it.
# The order tie-break (§6.1) uses the real creadaEn; the order key uses
# reanudadaEn as creadaEn.
# "I resume the task on <resumed>" taps Reanudar in the panel at that moment.
# "the task was paused" is a task already paused before any other
# date of the scenario. Progress is a fraction between 0 and 1, compared
# exactly.
# Reference week: Monday 2026-07-13 to Sunday 2026-07-19.
Feature: Resume task

  # Resume task 1
  # Relative: on resume it is pending, regardless of the completion from
  # before the pause (row 1: without the rule it would be waiting; row 2:
  # overdue), and it does not become overdue as long as it is not completed (row 3).
  Scenario Outline: Resume task 1
    Given a relative recurring task every <every> <unit>
    And the task was completed on <completed>
    And the task was paused
    When I resume the task on <resumed>
    And I query the status on <now>
    Then the task is not paused
    And the status is pendiente

    Examples:
      | every | unit   | completed           | resumed             | now                 |
      | 2    | dias   | 2026-07-15T09:00:00 | 2026-07-15T10:00:00 | 2026-07-15T10:00:00 |
      | 2    | dias   | 2026-07-01T09:00:00 | 2026-07-15T10:00:00 | 2026-07-15T10:00:00 |
      | 4    | horas  | 2026-07-14T09:00:00 | 2026-07-15T10:00:00 | 2026-07-20T10:00:00 |

  # Resume task 2
